WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.137
Professional analytics is not only about code quality.

00:00:03.137 --> 00:00:06.027
It is also about responsible data handling.

00:00:06.027 --> 00:00:13.957
Some data can identify people directly, such as names, email addresses, phone numbers, or IDs.

00:00:13.957 --> 00:00:18.862
Other data can become identifying when combined with additional information.

00:00:18.862 --> 00:00:21.832
A good practice is data minimization.

00:00:21.832 --> 00:00:24.757
Keep only the data needed for the task.

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:27.187
Another practice is masking.

00:00:27.187 --> 00:00:31.432
If we do not need to show the full value, we can hide part of it.

00:00:31.432 --> 00:00:38.217
In the code example, the function mask_email keeps the first letter of the username and the domain,

00:00:38.217 --> 00:00:40.732
but hides the rest of the username.

00:00:40.732 --> 00:00:43.607
This is only a simple demonstration.

00:00:43.607 --> 00:00:49.492
Real privacy requirements depend on the context, institution, and data type.

00:00:49.492 --> 00:00:54.347
But the general habit is important: do not expose sensitive data unless there is a clear reason and

00:00:54.347 --> 00:00:57.328
permission to do so.
